# Cmd+Enter runs an example. Copy any block into your file.

@baseUrl = https://httpbin.org


### Simplest request
GET https://httpbin.org/get

### Headers and a body
# A blank line separates the body.
POST {{baseUrl}}/post
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Anya"}

### Long URLs
GET {{baseUrl}}/get
    ?page=1
    &limit=20

### No method means GET
httpbin.org/get


### File variables
@host = httpbin.org
GET https://{{host}}/get

### Environments
# respite.json, respite-dev.json,
# respite-dev.private.json (secrets):
#   {"token": "dev-token"}
GET {{baseUrl}}/bearer
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### OAuth 2.0
# Configured in an env file the same way as in JetBrains:
#   {"Security": {"Auth": {"api": {"Type": "OAuth2",
#     "Grant Type": "Client Credentials",
#     "Token URL": "https://demo.duendesoftware.com/connect/token",
#     "Client ID": "m2m", "Client Secret": "{{clientSecret}}",
#     "Scope": "api"}}}}
# Grants: Client Credentials, Password,
#   Authorization Code ("Auth URL", "PKCE": true; opens the browser),
#   Device Authorization ("Device Auth URL"; shows the code to enter);
#   "Type": "Mock" for tests.
# The token is fetched once, cached, refreshed near expiry.
# $auth.idToken("api") for the ID token.
GET https://demo.duendesoftware.com/api/test
Authorization: Bearer {{$auth.token("api")}}

### Generated values
# Offsets: y M w d h m s ms.
# Also: $processEnv HOME, $dotenv KEY, $localDatetime.
POST {{baseUrl}}/post
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": "{{$uuid}}",
  "n": {{$randomInt 1 100}},
  "unix": {{$timestamp}},
  "iso": "{{$isoTimestamp}}",
  "day": "{{$datetime "YYYY-MM-DD"}}",
  "nextWeek": "{{$datetime iso8601 7 d}}"
}


### Log in
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/post
Content-Type: application/json

{"token": "abc123"}

### Use login's response
# Runs login first if needed.
# Also: response.headers.X, response.body.*, request.body.
GET {{baseUrl}}/bearer
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.json.token}}


### Directives
# @timeout 10 s
# @connection-timeout 2 s
# @no-redirect
# @no-cookie-jar
# @no-log
GET {{baseUrl}}/redirect/1

### Self-signed certificate
# @insecure
GET https://self-signed.badssl.com/

### Client certificate (mTLS)
# In respite-<env>.private.json, for every request of that env:
#   {"SSLConfiguration": {
#     "clientCertificate": "certs/client.pem",
#     "clientCertificateKey": "certs/client.key",
#     "caCertificate": "certs/dev-ca.pem",
#     "verifyHostCertificate": true}}
# PEM or DER; paths relative to the env file.
# Proxy: the system one, or Settings → Requests.
GET https://client.badssl.com/

### Ask for a value
# @prompt otp One-time code
POST {{baseUrl}}/post

{"otp": "{{otp}}"}

### Confirm before sending
# @note Deletes for real
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/delete

### Assertions
# Results in the Tests tab; `respite run` exits 1 when one fails.
# Subjects: status, header <name>, body, body <JSONPath>, duration.
# Operators: == != < <= > >= contains startsWith endsWith matches
#   exists isTrue isFalse isNumber isString isBoolean isArray
# Comments to other clients, so the file still runs in VS Code and JetBrains.
# @assert status == 200
# @assert header content-type contains json
# @assert body $.json.name == Ann
# @assert body json.tags isArray
# @assert duration < 2 s
POST {{baseUrl}}/post
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Ann", "tags": ["a"]}


### Body from a file
# <@ fills {{variables}} in the file, < sends it as is.
POST {{baseUrl}}/post
Content-Type: application/json

< ./payload.json

### Form
POST {{baseUrl}}/post
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

user=anya
&city=Kyiv

### File upload
POST {{baseUrl}}/post
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=B

--B
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="report.pdf"

< ./report.pdf
--B--

### GraphQL
GRAPHQL https://countries.trevorblades.com/

query Country($code: ID!) {
  country(code: $code) { name capital }
}

{"code": "UA"}

### Basic auth
GET {{baseUrl}}/basic-auth/anya/secret
Authorization: Basic anya secret

### Save the response
# >>! overwrites.
GET {{baseUrl}}/json

>> ./out/sample.json
